  "namesake_notes": "Jesuit shelf: all Ignatius of Loyola (founder). Thomas Christians: Ignatius Loyola, Mar Ignatius (Jacobite prelate of 1653 / patriarchs titled Ignatius), Ignatius Aichamoni. Ethiopian synaxarium: patriarch lists (Antioch/Alexandria, 'Ignatius I-XXVI'). Melkite: Ignatius Giohar, Ignatius Saruff, patriarch Ignatius of 1700s.",
  "editorial_notes": "Ethiopian ctx 3-17: patriarch tables printed by Budge (editorial appendix lists, 'Ignatius died 107' in a table with Lequien/Assemani citations).",
  "comment": "Ignatius of Antioch is reached only in the Ethiopian synaxarium notice (v2-v4 file lines 5860-5950, also 38479, 39615-39632 in the same file; the later notice calls him 'Archbishop of Rome', conflated) and once each in Philipos (Q.? line 1598, translator gloss '(Ignatius)' on Ignatheous) and a Latin Melkite document (Mansi 46 line 33664). Ethiopian count 2 is from contexts (opening and trial dialogue of one notice); no tradition reaches 5.",
  "passes": false
